      ],
      "source": "https://www.albemarlenc.gov/our-city/visitors/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on a site that has been inhabited for nearly 10,000 years by hunter‑gatherer and mound‑builder tribes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albemarle%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1891 the Yadkin Railroad brought rail service to Albemarle, and a decade later the Winston‑Salem Southbound Railway built its own line, shaping the town’s textile boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albemarle%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Albemarle earned National Trust for Historic Preservation’s National Main Street City designation in 1993, highlighting its well‑preserved downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albemarle%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Museum of the Albemarle, located downtown, promotes understanding of regional history and hosts the official North Carolina Shad Boat, built in the 1880s.",
